A3.4 · Build the pool: every distinct move that appears in ANY of the three sets. A move in only one list still goes in the pool. ^H4SkePBO

A3.7 asks the chess library whether the game is over,
using only a snapshot of the current position. A
snapshot carries no move history, so a draw by
threefold repetition can never be spotted here.
Replaying the moves instead would catch it. ^77z0TkMU

