The elite database is fetched and passed to the filter. The filter looks up the matching elite move but never uses the result. Elite data therefore cannot make a White move pass the filter. A move found only in the elite list enters the pool but is always dropped, because it has no amateur games and no master games.
 ^IRSXbEQc

A3.11 · When creating a new position-cache entry, ask Wikibooks for a text snippet if the move history is not empty. For an existing entry, ask only when all three are true: it has no opening name, it has no saved snippet, and the current masters result supplies an opening name. An empty move history always skips Wikibooks.
 ^KQDaoLZm

The opening name and code are available from the masters result only when the masters API is queried. Once all three move sets are cached, later visits use the local move cache, which stores no opening name or code. If the position-cache entry still lacks that information, A3.3 cannot fill it in.
 ^XZixsMoM

